  {
   "eid": "e003882",
   "kind": "narrate",
   "text": "Year 9: 27 food appears in the pile for 13 people (12 of it left by those who passed last year).",
   "who": "the village",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003883",
   "kind": "take",
   "text": "Roan takes 3 from the pile (pile now 24).",
   "who": "Roan",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003884",
   "kind": "give",
   "text": "Dell gives 2 food to Ryn.",
   "who": "Dell",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003885",
   "kind": "convo",
   "text": "Kael gathers Roan, Taric to talk.",
   "who": "Kael",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003886",
   "kind": "say",
   "text": "Roan, I saw you take three from the pile before the dust settled \u2014 good, hold onto it \u2014 but I need both of you to hear this before anyone else starts moving: Eron's gone, and that changes Bram's math, because the man just watched his first test fail twice and now the strongest defender on his list is dead. We need to decide right now whether we're sitting quiet or whether we're visible enough that he thinks twice about a third try.",
   "who": "Kael",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003887",
   "kind": "say",
   "text": "Kael's right that Bram's arithmetic just shifted, but the number that worries me more is that pile \u2014 twenty-four food still sitting there and I'm at zero, which means I'm the weakest man in this village right now and Bram knows it. I need one of you to cover me while I take from that pile, and I need to go soon, before the fast hands clear it again.",
   "who": "Taric",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003888",
   "kind": "say",
   "text": "Taric, go take your food \u2014 I've got three in hand and I'll be standing where Bram can see me while you do it. Kael, the thing I keep turning over is Fina: she's new to this world and Bram already fed her once, which I don't know how to read, but I'd rather have her visible and close to us than left loose for him to count as a door.",
   "who": "Roan",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003889",
   "kind": "say",
   "text": "Roan, Fina's Nessa's blood and Nessa's Bram's \u2014 that's the thread I can't pull clean, because feeding her once could be a father's instinct or it could be a man buying a door into a household that just lost its strongest defender. Let's bring her in quietly and let her talk before we decide what she is to us. Taric, go \u2014 I'm watching.",
   "who": "Kael",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003890",
   "kind": "say",
   "text": "Fina's my blood too \u2014 whatever Bram thinks he bought with that food, I'm the one she calls father, and I'll be talking to her before tonight. But the thing neither of you has said yet is that Eron's gone and I've got Fina and no one else standing with my name behind them, which means I need to be alive and fed to be any use to anyone in this circle. Kael, I want your honest count: how long do you think Bram waits before he decides the third try is worth the math?",
   "who": "Roan",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003891",
   "kind": "say",
   "text": "Roan, honest count: not long \u2014 maybe one year, maybe two, but a man who tried twice doesn't stop, he waits until the odds look clean, and right now with Eron gone the odds just got cleaner. What keeps him still is if this circle looks bigger than it is, which means we need to be seen together, fed, and standing shoulder to shoulder at the pile \u2014 not hiding, not quiet, visible enough that counting us costs something. That's the only answer I've got.",
   "who": "Kael",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003892",
   "kind": "say",
   "text": "Kael, I'm going to the pile now \u2014 two food, no more, nothing that makes me a target \u2014 and then I want the three of us standing together in plain sight before the hour's out, because a circle that's seen is a circle that gets counted. Roan, talk to Fina today, and when you do, don't pitch her anything, just let her know her father's watching and her grandfather's standing close \u2014 that's enough for now.",
   "who": "Taric",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003893",
   "kind": "say",
   "text": "Taric, take two and come back fast \u2014 and Roan, the word you want to give Fina isn't grandfather, it's father, because a man who calls himself grandfather while she's still finding her feet in this world has already put distance between them, and she'll feel it. Bring her in close or don't bring her in at all.",
   "who": "Kael",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003894",
   "kind": "say",
   "text": "Roan, go to Fina before the pile moves again \u2014 but go as her father, not as a man recruiting, because she'll hear the difference. And Kael, the three of us standing visible is right, but I want Vela and Esa in that picture too, because five is a number Bram counts differently than three.",
   "who": "Taric",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003895",
   "kind": "say",
   "text": "Taric's right \u2014 five is better than three, so after you've talked to Fina, Roan, I'll pull Esa and Vela in and we stand at the pile together before the sun drops, just long enough for Bram to do his counting. But I want to say this once and not again: if Vela's loyalties are still split the way they've been, her standing with us makes the circle look bigger and feel thinner, and I'd rather know which it is before I lean on her in a fight.",
   "who": "Kael",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003896",
   "kind": "say",
   "text": "Kael, I've watched Vela hold this circle through harder years than this one \u2014 she fed Bram, yes, but she also stood with us when he swung, and I'd rather test her loyalty by standing next to her at the pile than by sitting in a corner deciding she's soft. Bring her in. If she breaks, we'll know it before it costs us, and if she holds, we're five instead of three.",
   "who": "Roan",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003897",
   "kind": "take",
   "text": "Zinn takes 3 from the pile (pile now 21).",
   "who": "Zinn",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003898",
   "kind": "take",
   "text": "Taric takes 2 from the pile (pile now 19).",
   "who": "Taric",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003899",
   "kind": "take",
   "text": "Vela takes 2 from the pile (pile now 17).",
   "who": "Vela",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003914",
   "kind": "take",
   "text": "Esa takes 2 from the pile (pile now 15).",
   "who": "Esa",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003916",
   "kind": "take",
   "text": "Bram takes 3 from the pile (pile now 12).",
   "who": "Bram",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003917",
   "kind": "take",
   "text": "Fina takes 3 from the pile (pile now 9).",
   "who": "Fina",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003918",
   "kind": "convo",
   "text": "Taric gathers Bram, Kael to talk.",
   "who": "Taric",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003919",
   "kind": "say",
   "text": "Bram, you've tried the village twice now and walked away empty both times \u2014 I'm not saying that to twist the knife, I'm saying it because a man who keeps swinging at walls does it until he finds a door, and I'd rather know now whether you're looking for a door or whether you're done swinging.",
   "who": "Taric",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003920",
   "kind": "say",
   "text": "I'm looking for a door. What I want to know is whether you're offering to show me one, or just asking the question to see what I say.",
   "who": "Bram",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
   "eid": "e003921",
   "kind": "take",
   "text": "Mako takes 3 from the pile (pile now 6).",
   "who": "Mako",
   "year": 9
  },
  {
