 "memory_summary": "Year 1, I pulled Ryn, Sela, and Esa into a circle early \u2014 we named Bram and Dav as threats, and Ryn told us Dav had already come to her alone with soft words. She stayed quiet about the details, which I filed away. Taric gave Esa a food unprompted, which counted for something.\n\nYear 2, I widened the circle to include Vela. We each swore plainly \u2014 I said I'd bleed with them, they said the same back \u2014 and that promise sat heavier than most words in this village. Esa went to Taric and he gave her food; we counted him ours. Ryn finally named it: Dav had offered her a child. We told her to decide before she answered him, but she'd already decided, because Dell was born before the year was out. Dav gave Dell food; Taric gave Esa food; Ryn fed her own child twice from her own hands. Those debts I noted.\n\nWhat I remember most: Bram and Mako moved in pairs off the pile two years running and never said a word to any of us. Mako's silence still sits like a stone in my chest. And Ryn \u2014 she's in our circle, she bled with us in word, but she made a child with a man none of us fully trust. The question of where Dav's loyalty actually runs is the one I haven't stopped asking. Year 3: Bram moved on Roan \u2014 the whole circle turned out against him and he backed down. That moment felt like proof we were real. But Ryn never gave us a clean answer about Dav, and he spent the whole year feeding her hand to mouth like a man keeping something he doesn't trust on a short leash. Eron was born to Sela and Roan, and I noted Roan had planted a root.\n\nYear 4: Vela started bleeding food to Bram \u2014 three times over while sitting in our circle and saying nothing. I called it out twice in front of everyone. She never answered. The circle held, but something cracked in it, and I felt myself start planning around her instead of with her.\n\nYear 5: Sela had a child with Bram \u2014 Nessa, born the same hour Mako handed Sela food, which is not coincidence. We circled Sela half a dozen times asking what Mako wanted from her and she gave us nothing but silence. I threatened to step aside. The threat landed like a stone in still water and sank without a ripple. Whatever Mako bought from her, she kept it.\n\nWhat sits heaviest: Ryn broke with us and joined Dav's attack on Esa in year six \u2014 a woman I bled with in word since year one, turned raider. Dav starved before the year closed, which is the only justice I've seen. The circle I built is smaller and thinner than it was, and the cracks are named: Vela's loyalty is borrowed, Sela's is mortgaged, and Ryn I've stopped counting. Ryn had been in my circle since year one, sworn in words \u2014 and then in year six she walked into Dav's attack on Esa alongside Dell, and I watched her stand there while Esa submitted and Dav took her food. That broke something I won't name as grief exactly, but it sits like grief. Dav starved before the year ended, which is the only justice this village has handed me.\n\nVela I confronted three times, plainly and in front of witnesses, about feeding Bram. She never answered. Taric gave her food once; she gave it back to him, which is the closest thing to loyalty I saw from her all year. I've stopped expecting more.\n\nMako planted his third root when Zinn was born to him and Sela \u2014 on top of Eron through Roan and Nessa through Bram. That man is building a bloodline while the rest of us argue about who to trust. Roan's his own thread into that household and I've pulled it, but gently.\n\nTaric and Esa have been feeding each other quietly for two years now, and I've watched it without naming it, because it's the kind of thing that either becomes something real or doesn't, and either way it's theirs.\n\nThe food flows between Ryn and Dell \u2014 back and forth, hand to hand \u2014 are the only thing those two do that I understand completely. They're each other's whole world now, and I'm not in it. Taric is dead \u2014 starved at fifty-three, the same man I fed twice with my own hand and watched make a child with Esa in year eight, witnessed by Roan and me. That child exists somewhere in this village's blood and I don't know yet what it means without him standing behind it.\n\nBram tried twice and walked away empty both times \u2014 once at Eron, once at Vela \u2014 but Eron's dead now anyway, which is the only victory Bram's gotten without swinging. Roan lost his son and I lost the strongest body behind my name, and those two facts are the same fact.\n\nVela fed Bram food across years without ever explaining herself to me, and I've stopped expecting an explanation. She's in the circle when numbers count and gone from it when words do.\n\nEsa and Taric made a child in year eight. I stood witness. Ryn broke with me in year six \u2014 stood beside Dav while he took from Esa \u2014 and I've counted her gone since. Dav starved; that's all the justice I got.\n\nMako has roots through Sela, through Nessa by way of Bram, through Zinn of his own blood. He is building something and I am still standing as a person instead of a bloodline, which is the thing I haven't solved and the thing that will kill me if I don't.",
